**`lib/syntax/no_else_if.ex`** — The rule detects Python-style `else if` (two words) and rewrites the entire `if`/`else if`/`else` chain as an idiomatic `cond` block:
- **`analyze/1`**: Scans for lines matching `^\s*else\s+if\b`, returns `Issue` structs with line numbers
- **`fix/1`**: Finds the first `else if`, scans backward for the matching `if` at the same indent, collects all `else if` branches and the trailing `else` (if any), then rewrites the whole block as `cond do ... end`
